  "articleBody": "Knowing when it's time to refinish your log or cabin home can save you a lot of headache and expense down the road. You really don't want to wait until the finish has completely failed, as that can lead to more serious issues. A key thing to look for is how your logs react to water. If water isn't beading up and instead soaks into the wood, that's a big red flag. Another tell-tale sign is fading, especially on those south and west-facing walls that get the most sun. Beyond that, keep an eye out for peeling or flaking on the existing finish. If the wood itself starts to look rough, splintered, or discolored, particularly turning gray, it's definitely time to think about a refresh. These are all indicators that your cabin's protective layer is wearing thin and it’s no longer doing its job. Catching these early can make the refinishing process smoother and help protect your investment for years to come. If you're seeing any of these signs, it's worth having a professional take a look. We're here to help you keep your cabin looking its best.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
